{"name":"Cultured Rose","hex":"#e5867b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cultured","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Learned in the ways of civilized society; civilized; refined.","Artificially developed."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of culture"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cultured"},{"term":"rose","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shrub of the genus Rosa, with red, pink, white or yellow flowers.","A flower of the rose plant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make rose-colored; to redden or flush.","To perfume, as with roses."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rose"}],"entries":[{"title":"Culture","blocks":[{"text":"Culture is a concept that encompasses the social behavior, institutions, and norms found in human societies, as well as the knowledge, beliefs, arts, laws, customs, capabilities, attitudes, and habits of the individuals in these groups. Culture often originates from or is attributed to a specific region or location."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/9_Bisonte_Magdaleniense_pol%C3%ADcromo.jpg/330px-9_Bisonte_Magdaleniense_pol%C3%ADcromo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Culture","wikidata":"Q11042"},{"title":"Rose","blocks":[{"text":"A rose is either a woody perennial flowering plant of the genus Rosa, in the family Rosaceae, or the flower it bears. There are over three hundred species and tens of thousands of cultivars. The plants range in size and form, from trailing and erect shrubs to climbers up to 7 metres (23 ft) in height. Sharp prickles appear on the stems of many species. Their flowers vary in size and shape and are usually large and showy, in colours ranging from white through pinks, reds, oranges and yellows."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg/330px-Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose","wikidata":"Q34687"},{"title":"Rose (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Rose is the color halfway between red and magenta, whose hue corresponds to an angle of 330 degrees on the HSV/HSL color wheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg/330px-Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_(color)","wikidata":"Q533047"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Singapore._Sri_Mariamman._Gopuram._South_East-19.JPG/500px-Singapore._Sri_Mariamman._Gopuram._South_East-19.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Singapore._Sri_Mariamman._Gopuram._South_East-19.JPG/1280px-Singapore._Sri_Mariamman._Gopuram._South_East-19.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Singapore._Sri_Mariamman._Gopuram._South_East-19.JPG/500px-Singapore._Sri_Mariamman._Gopuram._South_East-19.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASingapore._Sri_Mariamman._Gopuram._South_East-19.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Volksfestumzug_in_Vilshofen_a.d._Donau_2012_%283%29.JPG/500px-Volksfestumzug_in_Vilshofen_a.d._Donau_2012_%283%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Volksfestumzug_in_Vilshofen_a.d._Donau_2012_%283%29.JPG/1280px-Volksfestumzug_in_Vilshofen_a.d._Donau_2012_%283%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedi